  "goodToKnow": "Die Berufsausbildung is vocational training. Germany's famous duales System combines on-the-job training in a company with classes at a Berufsschule, usually for two to three and a half years. There are around 320 recognised training occupations, from Bäcker to Mechatroniker. Trainees are called Auszubildende, or Azubis, and are paid. The system is often credited with Germany's low youth unemployment. Plural: die Berufsausbildungen."
